## Key Learnings

* SOC detection systems require architecture-level thinking: ingestion reliability, storage strategy, and integrity controls matter as much as detection logic
* Context enrichment (identity/asset baselines/history) is a first-class architectural layer, not an optional enhancement
* Detection must be explainable and workflow-aligned to preserve analyst trust and reduce alert fatigue
* Without feedback loops (analyst outcomes), detection rules and baselines decay over time

